{"skill":{"slug":"read-word","displayName":"Read Microsoft Word documents (.docx and .doc) with Chinese support"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1773995587157,"changelog":"read-word v1.0.0\n\n- Initial release with support for both .docx and legacy .doc Word formats\n- Full Chinese language encoding support\n- Keyword search across document paragraphs\n- Save extracted text as UTF-8 text files\n- No Microsoft Word installation required","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"README.md","size":820,"sha256":"ca600ebf105fd836d1b79f99c62807a307d82db5076addce9984904133fd12e4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"read_word.py","size":6880,"sha256":"e345cb7c0d6e04d7fe17c71088e5ed339af6cc2baf21335d97183d6d4314f8a9","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":34,"sha256":"c54fe7b235185009b96e7701b7d15fbafb74b563c1724a7508e371185f2a9e08","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5173,"sha256":"046985a8b631188eaf136676df5514225f06c5f653381d37a0f8ea8dbbbbadb4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":652,"sha256":"18e69facdaa5d74b9ad2ef86c00354cf6e56d30cffc00187779c7741a7d38d24","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"__init__.py","size":672,"sha256":"a10fcd1c5bfc6f364f664bd51d17ebde87115ee578c2e7fa6da8dc3f5cfa80c4","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2252,"sha256":"2e51e35839d1308a2d77947a010bf95f44b5baee49aa783ff3351ff4a8331e89","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789202793505,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"6ed96df80e43eec12d9596126cd33bfbaee68f43f4afdd4b7d8dbebb2725c71b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/6ed96df80e43eec12d9596126cd33bfbaee68f43f4afdd4b7d8dbebb2725c71b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086334228},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":37,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789202793505},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a local Word document reader with optional user-directed text export and no evidence of hidden network, persistence, credential access, or destructive behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill reads only user-provided Word document paths and writes only when the user supplies an output path. It declares no network need and the code contains no network calls.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation asks users to install two PyPI dependencies and copy the skill into an OpenClaw skills directory. Dependencies use lower-bound version constraints rather than exact pins, which is a supply-chain reproducibility concern but not evidence of malicious behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are ordinary command-line and Python API examples for user-specified files. No prompt hijacking, role changes, hidden agent instructions, or unrelated workflow control were found.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No services, scheduled tasks, hooks, memory writes, credential/session use, privilege escalation, or persistent background behavior were found. Persistence is limited to normal installation files and optional output text files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to read .docx/.doc files, search text, analyze basic document stats, and optionally export extracted text; the implementation matches that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Reasonable to install if you need local Word document text extraction. Treat Word files from untrusted sources carefully because document parsers can have vulnerabilities, and consider pinning dependency versions before production use. Use --output only with paths you intend to create or overwrite.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The optional --output write behavior is purpose-aligned text export and is disclosed in SKILL.md, though _meta.json lists only file-read capability; this is a metadata clarity gap, not a material Review concern.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-language documentation and Chinese support are visible and aligned with the stated document-reading purpose; no forced locale behavior, deception, or security-relevant user impact was found.\n[SQP-1] expected: The manifest description is broad but accurately describes a Word-reading skill; routing ambiguity is minor because the artifact's instructions and entry point are narrowly scoped.\n[SC1] expected: python-docx and olefile are expected dependencies for parsing Word documents, but they are not pinned exactly, so users should prefer reviewed pinned versions or a lockfile for reproducible installs.\n[SC4] expected: The python-docx dependency has a lower bound of >=0.8.11, which is above the historical vulnerable pre-0.8.6 range cited by the scanner; unpinned future resolution remains a maintenance risk but not a malicious signal.\n[AIG SARIF] expected: The A.I.G scan reported no T01-T09 results, consistent with manual inspection finding no hijacking, remote payload retrieval, embedded malicious code, persistence, or privilege escalation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789202793505}}}}}